  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ensuring the Support for the Rohingya Refugees Affected by the Fire in March 2023</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">On 5 March 2023 between 14h50 and 17h00, a massive and devastating fire broke out in Rohingya refugee Camp 11 in Cox&#x2019;s Bazar, Bangladesh. The fire was soon contained by local fire fighters and local authorities, however, over 2,800 shelters were fully or partially damaged, affecting some 16,000 individuals (approx. 3,011 families), including 5,274 individuals displaced to surrounding areas. Immediate needs included food, water, health, sanitation, and protection. Through this project, IOM is prioritize scaling up existing interventions in Shelter/non-food items (NFI), Site Management and Site Development (SMSD), and Water, Sanitation, and Hygiene (WASH).</narrative>
  </description>
